\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Free sign and clock frames}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{For the real sign orbit with reference value #{1}, the frame at
#{x} is #{\phi_x}. Hence the [reduced link](fdip-010X) is
#{\check U_e=\phi_{h(e)}U_e\phi_{s(e)}}. The exponential hopping
factor is #{\ue^{w_e\check U_e}}. Given the reduced links, each
choice of the site signs recovers the original links by the same
three-sign product. Thus the sign model counts each reduced tuple
#{2^{|X|}} times.}

\p{Use the cyclic group of #{N\ge2} rotations of a real plane and
the regular clock orbit of \ref{fdip-00ZX}. In rotation steps
modulo #{N}, write #{j_x} for the scalar position and #{\ell_e}
for the original link. With reference position zero the reduced
link has step #{\ell_e+j_{s(e)}-j_{h(e)}}. Its hopping factor is
##{\ue^{w_e\cos(2\pi(\ell_e+j_{s(e)}-j_{h(e)})/N)}.}
Given the scalar positions, subtracting the source step and adding
the head step recovers the original link. Hence the counting factor
is #{N^{|X|}}.}
